From: Chandler Newman <chandler2newman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fs/dax: do not derive a folio from a zero or empty entry

dax_associate_entry(), dax_disassociate_entry() and dax_busy_page() call
dax_to_folio() before testing the entry for the zero and empty cases,
so the result is computed for entries that have no page behind them.

dax_to_folio() is page_folio(pfn_to_page(dax_to_pfn(entry))), and
page_folio() dereferences page->compound_head. An empty entry yields
pfn 0, so on arm64 pfn_to_page(0) is VMEMMAP_START biased by
memstart_addr; with memstart_addr non-zero that address lies below the
start of the vmemmap in an unmapped hole, and the read of
compound_head faults:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address fffffdffbf000008
  Call trace:
    dax_disassociate_entry+0x1c/0x88
    __dax_invalidate_entry+0x9c/0x100

A virtio-fs mount with a DAX window reaches this on the first
invalidation of an entry that was never mapped, which makes it a boot
failure rather than a corner case.

Compute the folio only once the entry is known to have a page.

Signed-off-by: Chandler Newman <chandler2newman@gmail.com>
---
 fs/dax.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/fs/dax.c
+++ b/fs/dax.c
@@ -443,11 +443,13 @@
 				unsigned long address, bool shared)
 {
 	unsigned long size = dax_entry_size(entry), index;
-	struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
+	struct folio *folio;
 
 	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
 		return;
 
+	folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
+
 	index = linear_page_index(vma, address & ~(size - 1));
 	if (shared && (folio->mapping || dax_folio_is_shared(folio))) {
 		if (folio->mapping)
@@ -468,21 +470,23 @@
 static void dax_disassociate_entry(void *entry, struct address_space *mapping,
 				bool trunc)
 {
-	struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
+	struct folio *folio;
 
 	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
 		return;
 
+	folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
 	dax_folio_put(folio);
 }
 
 static struct page *dax_busy_page(void *entry)
 {
-	struct folio *folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
+	struct folio *folio;
 
 	if (dax_is_zero_entry(entry) || dax_is_empty_entry(entry))
 		return NULL;
 
+	folio = dax_to_folio(entry);
 	if (folio_ref_count(folio) - folio_mapcount(folio))
 		return &folio->page;
 	else
